Z||000008||FieroMontreal||11-21-2001||09:57 PM||||Why it's called PSX..<P>Sony was working with Nintendo to make an "add-on" for the SNES.. it would be a cd system that would plug into the SNES. This project was called PSX. I was sorta like "SNES-2" .. it was going to be their "new" system for the next generation of gaming. when the project was more then 60% complete Nintendo pulled the plug on the PSX project.. Sony was extreamly angry at Nintendo and decided to jump into the Game market. they Continued work on the PSX and made it so that it would work without the SNES.. Then When video game mags would talk about this "new sony system" they would call it PSX because that was the old name and no new name was given.<P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif">   <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
