Z||000016||Nashco||11-23-2001||01:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B>whatever happened with that enos lives thing sony was putting on all the orginal ps one games.  Did it actually mean Sony lives (enos backwards is sone, which sounds like sony) or didnt they ever say?<P>my psx has been dead for a while now, wont play cds anymore.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know that a lot of the first gen Playstations had a manufacturing defect.  I heard about it from some of my friends, but didn't think too much of it, until a guy at work was going to throw his system away because it didn't play stuff, was really glitchy.  Well, I took it from him and followed my friends' advice.  They said the first gen units could be flipped upside down and they'll play like brand new again.  Amazingly enough, it works!  I don't know how or why, but it did, and I was happy <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I got a free playstation out of it!<P>Something worth trying.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
