Z||000019||JohnnyK||12-04-2001||06:06 PM||||Formula: I doubt flipping it is going to help then..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>isthiswhereiputausername: I have a similar problem. I have a modchip that is part of the gameshark, so you have to put a real cd in, let it spin, then put a copied one in. I assume you know what I'm talking about. Anyways, now it reads the original fine, but when i try to put in the copied, it makes rythmic clicking noises. The upside down thing might work, but I'd rather not have to do that..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Anyways, nintendo's not going anywhere anytime soon.||||reg||1
Z||000020||isthiswhereiputausername?||12-04-2001||06:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Formula: I doubt flipping it is going to help then..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>isthiswhereiputausername: I have a similar problem. I have a modchip that is part of the gameshark, so you have to put a real cd in, let it spin, then put a copied one in. I assume you know what I'm talking about. Anyways, now it reads the original fine, but when i try to put in the copied, it makes rythmic clicking noises. The upside down thing might work, but I'd rather not have to do that..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Anyways, nintendo's not going anywhere anytime soon.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>What type of cdr are you using Johnny?  Gigastorage (futureshop) is the best for psxs and memorex is junk.. <P> also what program are you using to copy the game? <P>most newer games wont work with the gameshark anymore.. <P>also the reason some older psxs need to be turned upside down is due to the guides on the 1001 was made out of plastic and wore out quickly (then had to be put upside down to get the laser close again) <BR>new guides can be made easily and the guides on the enwer psxs are made out of metal.<P>when you are hearing clicking, it means your laser is not spinning fast enough to load the game.   it sounds like your psx laser is out of adjustment. I can give you details to you for alligning the laser if you want..(just pm me)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000021||Adrift||12-05-2001||02:03 AM||||there's a lot of talk about 32bit/64bit/128bit systems going on here - how many "bits" the system is rated as doesn't determine how good the system is - video game system design & programming (Any hardware level-programming for that matter) is an INCREDIBLY COMPLEX science which can't be simply can not be simplified into saying "This system is 128, and therefore better then a 64 system", because there are SO many other factors which come into play. <P>It's very unusual to read Gamepro or other video game magazine where the author of an article actually knows something about computer hardware and exactly how it works. 99% of the time I find they are just copying information out of the manufacturers press release. ||||reg||1
